    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d508-a3">

                <pb facs="0931" n="871" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg871"/>

                <head>Mr. Hovey to Rear-Admiral
                        Turner.</head>
                <opener>
                    <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                        States.</hi></placeName></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Admiral:</hi> Do not fail to do all you can
                    to alleviate the sufferings of those who have borne the terrible calamity of the
                    late earthquake in Peru. I not only request but beg you to leave no effort
                    undone that may aid them in the hour of their direst calamity. If necessary,
                    make your vessels like merchantmen, to take food and provisions to those who may
                    now be suffering. Tell me how many medical men and assistants may be able to
                    find passage in the Powhatan to-morrow. I know your generous nature, and I am
                    sure our government will fully sanction all that you can do in the great cause
                    of humanity.</p>
                <p>I am, my dear admiral, yours very truly,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. P. HOVEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Rear-Admiral <hi rendition="#small-caps">T. Turner,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Commanding South Pacific Squadron,</hi> Present.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
